Autumn data






ExerciseExercise 7 - Repeat for autumn data






Extension
↑ top
In your worked_example.qmd Quarto document, repeat all of the steps above with your autumn_data data frame, to generate your own version of Figure 1A.






AnswerAnswer







min_lon &lt;- autumn_data |&gt;
  pull(Longitude) |&gt;
  min()

max_lon &lt;- autumn_data |&gt;
  pull(Longitude) |&gt;
  max()

min_lat &lt;- autumn_data |&gt;
  pull(Latitude) |&gt;
  min()

max_lat &lt;- autumn_data |&gt;
  pull(Latitude) |&gt;
  max()

ggplot(
  autumn_data,
  aes(x = Longitude, y = Latitude, color = Site, shape = Location_Type)
) +
  geom_point(size = 3) +
  annotation_borders(linewidth = 0.2) +
  coord_quickmap(
    xlim = c(min_lon - 2, max_lon + 2),
    ylim = c(min_lat - 2, max_lat + 2)
  ) +
  geom_path(aes(group = Site)) +
  ggtitle("Pied Flycatcher Autumn Migration Routes") +
  xlab("Longitude (°)") +
  ylab("Latitude (°)") +
  theme_minimal()
